-- title:
--   Diamond action on Gauss-reduced places of the Igusa field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and the intermediate field $K\subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image contains $\zeta$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$, $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ over $k$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (itself assumed proper), such that the $i_1,i_2$ cover every point of that fibre, the scheme-theoretic intersection $\operatorname{pullback} i_1\, i_2$ is reduced of cardinality $n>0$. Fix embeddings of $A$ and $L$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in a tower, a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) together with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto the base change of the two-chart model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ commuting with the structure maps, such that the preimage of the finite chart is nonempty and such that every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), read through $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection and transported by $M_\eta$.`ffEquiv`$^{-1}$, has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of that of $a$. Finally let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm k M` (a weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with integral $q$-expansion series whose reduction over $k$ is nonzero) and let $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ be a curve model over $k$ of the Igusa field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) with an isomorphism $e_1:\mathrm{Mdl}_1.C\cong C_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k$. The assertion is: for every $d$ coprime to $Mp$ there is a $k$-algebra automorphism $\delta$ of the Igusa field such that, for every valuation subring $\mathrm{Pl}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, every factorisation of $A\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ through $\mathrm{Pl}$ and through a subring $O$ with $\mathrm{Pl}\le O\le\mathrm{Pl}$, every surjection $\pi_k:\mathrm{Pl}\to k$ compatible with $A\to k$, and every map $\mathrm{red}_1$ from places of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of the Igusa field over $k$ which sends a place $P$ to the place attached by $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ to $c$ followed by $e_1^{-1}$ whenever $\xi$ is an $O$-integral point of the two-chart model extending the point of $P$ (through $M_\eta$.`pointEquivPlace`$^{-1}$, $e_\eta$ and the first projection) and $c$ is a $k$-point of $C_1$ whose image in the fibre is the $\pi_k$-reduction of $\xi$: for all places $P$ and $P_2$ with $P_2$ the image of $P$ under the semilinear automorphism attached to [`ModularCurve.diamondAutBar (M * p) d`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L94) (the field automorphism paired with the identity on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), if $P$ admits such a pair $(\xi,c)$ with $c$ avoiding the intersection $C_1\cap C_2$ and landing in the finite chart, then so does $P_2$, and $\mathrm{red}_1 P_2$ is the image of $\mathrm{red}_1 P$ under the semilinear automorphism attached to $\delta$. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$, not all of $F$, containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring, and the action is by taking images of valuation subrings.
--
--   This is the place-level statement that the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$ on $X_1(Mp)$ preserves the condition of reducing, at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$, to a point of the component $C_1$ of the special fibre lying off the nodes and inside the finite $j$-chart, and that its effect on the reduced places is realised by a single automorphism $\delta$ of the Igusa function field $k(X_1(M))(a)$ — no identification of $\delta$ being claimed. It is used in the subsequent step combining the diamond action with the Frobenius and Atkin–Lehner actions on finite sets of reduced places, in the analysis of the weight in the mod $p$ situation.
